{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: M1 host/install half at 432dab40a60a90bd0570e17ae7d73c17febb2986, tree 621efa82ff7652895bb6401713bbbd62bca95910. This is the complete review of child 873c8404 / d299657b, not closure of the M1 parent or deployment acceptance. Primary b02ae22d was read first and in full. All 153 changed paths were accounted for, with 153 unique fresh exact-head bindings in eight exhausted metadata queries. The extracted 2,187 regular Git blobs match their modes and object ids; 2,050 prior Main paths are unchanged. The 137 current source evidence files match the candidate, and all 16 deletions have exact baseline snapshots.\n\n1. Implementation and authority\n\nThe implementation follows c643756e, 866c7ae7, 0d973184, 716ace64 and 9075d42e. The exact opt-in register12/directory11/membership7/rules5/destination7 cohort records one admin-authorized install with retained semantic and signed-release proofs, exact declaration texts, original installer, explicit selected defaults and bounded genesis values. Package declarations alone add no grants. Native proof checks include canonical identities, publisher signature, whole-definition validation and exact detached text bindings before host work.\n\nThe host independently walks the immutable URI's commit, selected trees and regular blob, verifying object type, size and hash. No CLI upload, ref fallback, symlink/gitlink, redirect, credentials or subprocess substitutes for that walk. SHA-256 spelling remains in the codec; this host records unsupported-object-format before network. Exact operator release/publisher trust, signature/native admission and bounded canonical bytes precede the idempotent private R2 put. The admission operation only reads retained content. Recovery of fetch/storage is separately gated by the exact native catalog allowance; it does not grant a generic mutation-retry port.\n\nThe native phase sequence is fetch, admission, activation, grants and Directory-owned creation. A pre-admission refusal has no subordinate effects. A later definitive refusal remains final and records its phase and reason while earlier activation/grants remain in force; there is no rollback, synthetic signature or cross-scope transaction. Directory checks the actual Rules sibling, forwards selected additions to its actual Membership and creates the child with the original installer and actual destination. Unknown outcomes retain the original operation/envelope. Detached native declaration custody survives restart and removal of the screen object. Destination7's publication origin checks the Directory11 birth and actual sibling provenance; historical destination policies retain their separate branches.\n\nCLI and MCP share persistent custody, refuse changed meaning under a kept key, and reuse an accepted or uncertain original without fetching/signing a replacement. Native acknowledgement checks the exact receipt and recorded signed entry. Bounded status reads distinguish acceptance from pending, final refusal and active completion. The portable CLI uses an explicit runtime port. The canonical codecs moved below Platform to bytes/application with stable client exports; Platform has no client/transport dependency. MCP's exception is only service.ts importing git/application, and the broad/provider/Node edges remain refused.\n\nGeneric delivery checks the native Directory and active installation, exact presentation and current trust before serving named packet assets or public routing metadata. The route keeps HEAD, MIME, CSP, ETag/revalidation and no-fallback behavior. Pending cache loads count toward the two-entry allowance. Installed Counter and Lending bind invitations and private storage to the native incarnation, use actual Membership7 enrollment and nonextractable browser keys, retain verified-seat handoff before clearing join custody and restore identity after reload. Counter's refreshed preparation retry is restricted to definitely-unsent work; unknown requests retain their original, and reload does not rearm speech.\n\n2. Witnesses, controls and limits\n\nThe finite grant's map SHA-256 is 1b3f621db8d55a559738c192be245f30955b769fd09025a4e30d2e5c46ffa655. I verified and copied all 366 owned regular files (63,907,741 bytes), with no-follow/nonblocking opens, UID/link checks, stable file identity/metadata and exact hashes. All 28 explicit historical Git snapshots match their immutable blobs. No adjacent-directory, private dependency, credential, custody-key or provider access was taken from paths inside evidence.\n\nThe native witnesses exercise real scopes/SQLite/operation driver/R2/eviction/detached transport: fetch reply loss, crash before put, read-only admission recovery, CLI accepted-reply loss followed by a fresh CLI/MCP invocation, final untrusted/format refusals before network/effects, successful maintained definitions and late child refusal with prior grants retained. Whole native replay with proven grants, wrong proof/ref/authority controls, unchanged role preservation and capacity refusal support the claims. The pending-cache and narrow-import controls each fail at the intended assertion under the recorded fault and pass with the source restored.\n\nI read the complete final browser harness and its final result: Chromium 153.0.8010.12 / Playwright 1.63.0, fresh contexts, real browser-generated keys and native signed enrollment/application requests forwarded through Room's production entry, Counter participation/activation, Lending donation, identity restoration and all five changed journals replaying consistently with grants proven. I inspected the four final desktop/mobile PNGs. All 75 request records are accounted for; only the two explicitly unpublished shelf-page 404s occur, with no JavaScript or unexpected console errors. Git peer, repository creation host, clock and scheduler remain fixtures. This does not prove audio playback or a provider publication. The separate public GitHub transport witness is an exact 632-byte